WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:18.550
I'm alone in New York City, when I see you, please permit me to tell you everything, in New York City.
当我在纽约市独自一人看到你时，请允许我在纽约市把一切都告诉你。

2
00:00:20.250 --> 00:00:22.490
Welcome to How We Made Your Mother.
欢迎收看《我们是如何创造你母亲的》。

3
00:00:22.970 --> 00:00:24.290
I'm Josh Radner.
我是乔什·拉德纳。

4
00:00:25.030 --> 00:00:26.630
I'm here with Greg Thomas.
我和格雷格·托马斯在这里。

5
00:00:26.990 --> 00:00:27.770
Hi, Greg.
嗨，格雷格。

6
00:00:28.090 --> 00:00:28.650
Hello, Josh.
你好，乔什。

7
00:00:28.970 --> 00:00:31.410
We're just going to talk in a very short burst today.
我们今天将进行一次非常简短的对话。

8
00:00:31.410 --> 00:00:37.690
Yeah, we're talking about How I Met Your Mother, a show we made from 2005 to 2014.
对，我们在聊《老爸老妈浪漫史》，这部我们在2005年到2014年制作的剧集。

9
00:00:38.690 --> 00:00:42.310
Man, we are barreling along in season three.
天哪，我们在第三季里高歌猛进。

10
00:00:43.050 --> 00:00:44.990
We're almost at the end of season three.
我们快到第三季的尾声了。

11
00:00:45.310 --> 00:00:46.570
How many episodes are we doing?
我们要做多少集？

12
00:00:46.570 --> 00:00:47.470
We did 20 in this?
这一季我们做了20集吗？

13
00:00:47.490 --> 00:00:54.490
We're doing the last nine episodes of season three, fittingly, in the same very fast clip that they were shot.
我们正在制作第三季的最后九集，说来也巧，其节奏和它们拍摄时的速度一样非常快。

14
00:00:54.590 --> 00:01:00.770
They were shot nine episodes in 11 weeks, and we're kind of banging out the pod at the fastest rate we've ever done.
它们在11周内拍完了九集，而我们正在以我们做过的最快速度录制这个播客。

15
00:01:00.770 --> 00:01:04.610
And two, because of summer plans and summer travel, and it works.
其二是因为夏天的计划和夏天的旅行，而且这行得通。

16
00:01:04.650 --> 00:01:06.590
It is in alignment with the episodes themselves.
这与剧集本身保持了一致。

17
00:01:06.590 --> 00:01:10.070
Not too much time to think about it, which is what you guys did when you were writing it.
没有太多时间去思考，这正是你们当年在写剧本时所做的。

18
00:01:10.250 --> 00:01:11.470
Not too much time to think about it.
没有太多时间去思考。

19
00:01:11.830 --> 00:01:16.870
So today's episode is episode 18 of season three.
所以今天的剧集是第三季第18集。

20
00:01:17.010 --> 00:01:18.650
It's called Rebound Bro.
它叫《替代兄弟》。

21
00:01:18.690 --> 00:01:20.630
It was written by Jamie Rohnheimer.
它由杰米·罗恩海默编写。

22
00:01:20.830 --> 00:01:21.970
Was this Jamie's first episode?
这是杰米的第一集吗？

23
00:01:21.970 --> 00:01:25.350
No, Jamie Rohnheimer in season two wrote Aldrin Justice and Lucky Penny.
不，杰米·罗恩海默在第二季写过《奥尔德林的审判》和《幸运硬币》。

24
00:01:25.670 --> 00:01:31.730
And in this season, he wrote The Yips, and now he has written Rebound Bro.
而在这一季里，他写了《心理阴影》，现在他又写了《替代兄弟》。

25
00:01:31.950 --> 00:01:32.490
So here we are.
所以我们就到这里。

26
00:01:32.610 --> 00:01:33.150
Jamie Rohnheimer.
杰米·罗恩海默。

27
00:01:33.870 --> 00:01:38.970
My dog is making some noise in the room, and you will tell me if you want me to make her go out of the room.
我的狗在房间里弄出了一些动静，如果你想让我把它赶出房间，你会告诉我的。

28
00:01:39.030 --> 00:01:40.290
You'll tell me if you want me to put her down.
如果你想让我安乐死它，你会告诉我的。

29
00:01:41.610 --> 00:01:42.950
I think we've had a good run.
我觉得我们已经度过了一段美好的时光。

30
00:01:43.050 --> 00:01:43.670
She's already five.
它已经五岁了。

31
00:01:44.010 --> 00:01:45.070
It's just too much noise.
动静实在太大了。

32
00:01:45.190 --> 00:01:45.450
Five is the kind of weird.
五岁有点奇怪。

33
00:01:45.450 --> 00:01:46.030
You have to put her down.
你得把它安乐死。

34
00:01:48.610 --> 00:01:50.290
But yeah, so this is a very good, when did it air out?
不过是的，这是一部非常棒的剧，它是什么时候播出的？

35
00:01:50.370 --> 00:01:51.410
You just said the date.
你刚说了日期。

36
00:01:51.790 --> 00:01:52.730
May 5th, 2008.
2008年5月5日。

37
00:01:52.990 --> 00:01:53.610
May 5th.
5月5日。

38
00:01:53.730 --> 00:01:58.510
Man, we were just coming out of that Writer's Guild strike and just boom, start airing new episodes in March.
天哪，我们刚结束编剧协会罢工，然后轰的一声，三月份就开始播新剧集了。

39
00:01:58.710 --> 00:02:03.410
We were shooting episodes basically a week and a half before they'd be on the air, two weeks before.
我们拍剧集的时间基本上是在它们开播前一个半星期到两个星期。

40
00:02:03.850 --> 00:02:08.730
Everything about this was the most compressed time frame that we've ever had on the show.
关于这一点的一切都是我们在这部剧里经历过的最短时间框架。

41
00:02:09.470 --> 00:02:13.550
And I think a lot of good stuff weirdly came out of it, including this episode.
而且我觉得莫名其妙地从中诞生了很多好东西，包括这一集。

42
00:02:13.550 --> 00:02:19.070
You know what's funny is, like, in the first two seasons, it was always like, gosh, this was 19 years ago.
你知道有趣的是什么吗，就像在前两季里，总是觉得，天哪，这是19年前的事了。

43
00:02:19.210 --> 00:02:20.670
And somehow the math is working out.
不知何故，时间算下来了。

44
00:02:20.750 --> 00:02:22.950
It's like, well, now it's only 18 years ago.
就像是，好吧，现在它只有18年前了。

45
00:02:23.070 --> 00:02:25.190
Yeah, I think we're slowly closing the gap.
对，我想我们正在慢慢缩小差距。

46
00:02:26.710 --> 00:02:35.010
But yeah, so this, I really like this episode because this is, it was nice to create a condition in the previous episode.
不过是的，所以这个，我真的很喜欢这一集，因为这是一个，在上一集中创造一个条件感觉挺好的。

47
00:02:35.010 --> 00:02:41.270
It was good from a writing perspective and from a writing it in no time at all perspective to create this problem.
从写作的角度以及在极短时间内完成写作的角度来看，创造这个难题是很好的。

48
00:02:41.270 --> 00:02:44.670
The problem is, Barney and Ted, their friendship is over.
问题是，巴尼和泰德，他们的友谊结束了。

49
00:02:44.910 --> 00:02:46.370
They have had a bro breakup.
他们经历了一次兄弟分手。

50
00:02:47.010 --> 00:02:54.390
And I remember this episode, I think I may have come up with the phrase, Rebound Bro.
我记得这一集，我想我可能想出了“替代兄弟”这个短语。

51
00:02:54.650 --> 00:02:56.150
I think that may have been me.
我想那可能是我。

52
00:02:56.270 --> 00:02:57.710
If it was Jamie or somebody else, I apologize.
如果是杰米或其他什么人，我道歉。

53
00:02:58.030 --> 00:03:07.630
My memory of this is the rare, this was an instance where the title, Rebound Bro, we had two words and it was like, that's an entire episode.
我对这件事的记忆非常罕见，这是一个标题的例子，就是“反弹兄弟”，我们当时有两个词，然后就觉得，这就是整整一集。

54
00:03:07.630 --> 00:03:10.330
It unfolded very quickly.
它进展得非常快。

55
00:03:10.650 --> 00:03:15.830
And again, thank the creative gods, thank the writing gods, because we had no time to do it.
而且再次感谢创意之神，感谢编剧之神，因为我们根本没有时间去做这件事。

56
00:03:16.030 --> 00:03:19.690
And something about just going, this is what would happen next.
而且那种感觉就像是，接下来就会发生这种事。

57
00:03:19.810 --> 00:03:20.510
There's a problem.
有个问题。

58
00:03:20.950 --> 00:03:26.750
Barney would immediately want to fill the enormous crater in his life by not having Ted there anymore.
巴尼会立刻想要通过泰德不再那里的事实，来填补他生活中巨大的空白。

59
00:03:27.070 --> 00:03:28.990
And that there's a drive there.
而且那里有一种动力。

60
00:03:29.210 --> 00:03:31.430
Barney has to find a new wingman, go, that's the story.
巴尼必须找一个新的僚机，然后去，这就是故事。

61
00:03:31.950 --> 00:03:36.550
And then I think the Stella-Ted story is just as provocative.
然后我认为史黛拉和泰德的故事同样具有挑衅性。

62
00:03:36.950 --> 00:03:37.930
It's really juicy.
这真的很带劲。

63
00:03:38.110 --> 00:03:38.190
Yeah.
是啊。

64
00:03:38.310 --> 00:03:39.910
So what happens there?
那接下来发生什么？

65
00:03:40.510 --> 00:03:46.370
There, Ted learns that it has been five years since Stella has been intimate.
在那里，泰德得知史黛拉已经五年没有亲密行为了。

66
00:03:46.650 --> 00:03:47.790
She's a single mom.
她是一个单亲妈妈。

67
00:03:48.050 --> 00:03:49.250
His is five months.
他的是五个月。

68
00:03:49.570 --> 00:03:50.870
Yeah, he's at five months.
对，他的是五个月。

69
00:03:50.970 --> 00:03:53.090
He holds up five and she's like, I'm five years too.
他比出五，而她却说，我也是五年。

70
00:03:53.270 --> 00:03:55.290
And no, it's months for him and years for her.
不，对他是几个月，对她是几年。

71
00:03:55.670 --> 00:03:58.250
And that's juicy in and of itself, like five years.
这本身就很带劲，就像五年一样。

72
00:03:58.410 --> 00:03:58.930
That's interesting.
这很有趣。

73
00:03:58.930 --> 00:04:00.430
That's an interesting thing to discuss.
这是一件很有趣的讨论话题。

74
00:04:00.670 --> 00:04:04.010
She's a divorced mom of a girl she's very devoted to.
她是一个离婚的妈妈，带着一个她非常疼爱的女孩。

75
00:04:04.170 --> 00:04:07.230
She does not want to rush into anything stupid with the wrong guy.
她不想跟不对的人盲目冲动地开始任何事。

76
00:04:07.550 --> 00:04:08.730
Five years is a long time.
五年是很长的一段时间。

77
00:04:09.150 --> 00:04:12.610
And then Ted, in a weird way, breaks another sort of code, right?
然后泰德以一种奇怪的方式，又破坏了某种规则，对吧？

78
00:04:12.730 --> 00:04:14.770
He's forming this truSt.
他在建立这种信任。

79
00:04:15.030 --> 00:04:17.470
He's out on the outs with Barney because Barney broke the bro code.
他和巴尼闹翻了，因为巴尼破坏了兄弟准则。

80
00:04:17.710 --> 00:04:22.250
Ted kind of violates Stella's trust by telling Marshall and Lily about this five years thing.
泰德把这五年的事情告诉了马歇尔和莉莉，这有点违背了对斯特拉的信任。

81
00:04:22.250 --> 00:04:23.350
Although that's questionable.
尽管这还有待商榷。

82
00:04:23.350 --> 00:04:24.370
It's questionable, right.
确实有待商榷，对吧。

83
00:04:24.510 --> 00:04:25.650
I think it's a good debate.
我觉得这是个很好的辩论话题。

84
00:04:25.830 --> 00:04:28.830
It is a good debate because it was...
这确实是个好话题，因为它是……

85
00:04:28.930 --> 00:04:31.170
I actually was not mad at Ted in that instance.
说实话，在那件事上我并没有生泰德的气。

86
00:04:31.210 --> 00:04:32.470
I was mad at Marshall and Lily.
我生的是马歇尔和莉莉的气。

87
00:04:32.910 --> 00:04:34.490
I was like, why would you say that?
当时我就想，你们怎么能说那种话？

88
00:04:34.670 --> 00:04:35.370
They fucked that up.
他们把事情搞砸了。

89
00:04:35.450 --> 00:04:35.570
Yes.
是的。

90
00:04:35.670 --> 00:04:39.390
And that is, you could argue, some sitcom artifice that just spilled out.
你可以说，这完全是情景喜剧里为了推进剧情而生搬硬套出来的。

91
00:04:39.530 --> 00:04:42.750
That is maybe not the most realistic thing that would have happened.
这或许不是现实中可能发生的最真实的情况。

92
00:04:43.110 --> 00:04:43.370
Yeah.
没错。

93
00:04:43.430 --> 00:04:46.090
But again, we were underthinking this in the writing process.
但话又说回来，我们在创作过程中对这一点思考得不够深。

94
00:04:46.250 --> 00:04:47.710
We're like, problem, problem, problem.
我们当时的想法是，制造问题，制造问题，不断制造问题。

95
00:04:47.910 --> 00:04:48.910
The story is conflict.
故事就是冲突。

96
00:04:48.910 --> 00:04:49.350
Let's go.
我们上吧。

97
00:04:49.350 --> 00:04:55.890
I saw a guy do a video where he was like, a friend was telling him about that he was having an affair.
我看到过一个视频，里面有个男生说，有个朋友跟他坦白说自己有婚外情。

98
00:04:56.090 --> 00:04:57.750
Like, he was cheating on his wife.
也就是说，他出轨了。

99
00:04:57.950 --> 00:05:01.090
And they were friends with this guy and his wife.
而且他们和这个男的以及他的妻子都是好朋友。

100
00:05:01.210 --> 00:05:02.810
And he said, don't tell your wife.
然后他说，别告诉你老婆。

101
00:05:03.090 --> 00:05:07.990
And he wanted to say, like, that is the most ridiculous statement you could ever say to me.
而且他当时就像是想说，这简直是你对我说过最荒谬的话。

102
00:05:08.150 --> 00:05:09.350
Don't tell my wife.
别告诉我老婆。

103
00:05:09.470 --> 00:05:13.410
Like, I'm texting her under the table as you're telling me.
就在你跟我说的时候，我正在桌子底下给她发信息。

104
00:05:13.810 --> 00:05:15.270
Like, I'm telling her every...
我把每个...

105
00:05:15.270 --> 00:05:18.150
There's nothing I'm not telling her, so don't even say that.
没有什么是我没告诉她的，所以你别瞎扯。

106
00:05:18.470 --> 00:05:21.910
And I feel like in this gang, it's the same rules.
而且我觉得在这个小圈子里，也是一样的规矩。

107
00:05:22.210 --> 00:05:24.290
Like, I'm telling Marshall and Lily.
就像我正打算告诉马歇尔和莉莉一样。

108
00:05:24.590 --> 00:05:24.790
Yeah.
对。

109
00:05:24.950 --> 00:05:25.630
Like, I'm going to.
我就打算这么做。

110
00:05:25.850 --> 00:05:27.050
You don't know us well enough to know that.
你对我们还不够了解，所以不知道这一点。

111
00:05:27.050 --> 00:05:27.710
I'm on Team Ted on this one.
在这件事上我站泰德这边。

112
00:05:27.790 --> 00:05:31.010
I think Ted absolutely was always going to tell Marshall and Lily.
我觉得泰德绝对是一定会告诉马歇尔和莉莉的。

113
00:05:31.210 --> 00:05:32.950
Stella doesn't know them well yet.
史黛拉还不是很了解他们。

114
00:05:33.130 --> 00:05:33.970
They're just going to...
他们只会...

115
00:05:33.970 --> 00:05:36.750
So Stella doesn't know that dynamic, and she feels humiliated.
所以史黛拉并不了解这种动态，她感到受到了羞辱。

116
00:05:36.810 --> 00:05:38.050
No, it's humiliating for her.
不，这对她来说是一种羞辱。

117
00:05:38.150 --> 00:05:38.710
I get that.
我懂。

118
00:05:38.790 --> 00:05:39.850
I get why she's upset.
我理解她为什么不高兴。

119
00:05:40.050 --> 00:05:40.230
Yeah.
是啊。

120
00:05:40.410 --> 00:05:43.670
No, but she doesn't know that, of course, Ted was going to tell Marshall and Lily.
不对，但她不知道的是，泰德当然是打算告诉马歇尔和莉莉的。

121
00:05:43.670 --> 00:05:45.710
It's a fucking no-brainer that he was going to.
他绝对会这么做，这是用脚趾头都能想到的。

122
00:05:45.770 --> 00:05:49.850
And if Stella knew them even a little, she would know that that would happen and that
而且要是史黛拉对他们哪怕有一点了解，她就会知道这事会发生，并且

123
00:05:49.850 --> 00:05:51.130
she wouldn't feel as weird about it.
她也就不会觉得这事那么尴尬了。

124
00:05:51.190 --> 00:05:51.670
But she hasn't...
但她还没...

125
00:05:51.670 --> 00:05:53.850
She's barely even met Marshall and Lily at this point.
在这个时候，她甚至都没怎么见过马歇尔和莉莉。

126
00:05:54.090 --> 00:05:54.290
Yeah.
没错。

127
00:05:54.370 --> 00:05:58.710
And she feels mortified that they notice they do let this slip in a moment that is perhaps
而且他们居然在一个或许有点勉强的时机说漏了嘴，说实话，这让她感到极其难堪，

128
00:05:58.710 --> 00:06:01.030
slightly forced, if we're being honeSt.
如果我们坦诚一点的话。

129
00:06:01.350 --> 00:06:02.710
But it creates a good problem.
但这制造了一个不错的矛盾。

130
00:06:02.710 --> 00:06:07.770
And now she has an excuse to say that Ted has broken her trust and to take the step back,
现在她有了借口，可以说泰德辜负了她的信任并借此拉开距离，

131
00:06:07.890 --> 00:06:08.730
which is interesting.
这挺有意思的。

132
00:06:08.730 --> 00:06:13.930
And I also think Ted's parry, or counter, which is you're using this as an excuse to
而且我也觉得泰德的招架或反击——也就是你正借此

133
00:06:13.930 --> 00:06:14.630
create distance.
制造距离——

134
00:06:14.850 --> 00:06:16.590
Very smart and right on.
非常聪明，而且一针见血。

135
00:06:16.810 --> 00:06:16.910
Yeah.
对。

136
00:06:16.950 --> 00:06:17.090
Yeah.
对。

137
00:06:17.450 --> 00:06:18.070
Very smart.
非常聪明。

138
00:06:18.230 --> 00:06:19.510
And I love...
而且我喜欢...

139
00:06:19.510 --> 00:06:20.610
I like this.
我喜欢这个。

140
00:06:20.730 --> 00:06:24.250
I like that storyline a lot because, except for the part where Marshall and Lily let it
我非常喜欢这条故事线，因为除了马歇尔和莉莉说漏嘴的那部分——正如我们在编剧室里常说的那样，

141
00:06:24.250 --> 00:06:27.970
slip, which is a little sweaty, as we say in the writer's room, I think, but it still
那处理得有点生硬，但我认为它依然

142
00:06:27.970 --> 00:06:28.230
works.
行之有效。

143
00:06:28.230 --> 00:06:29.050
It needed to happen.
这必须发生。

144
00:06:29.170 --> 00:06:30.150
It needed to happen in the story.
这在剧情里是必须发生的。

145
00:06:30.250 --> 00:06:30.630
So you juSt...
所以你只能...

146
00:06:30.630 --> 00:06:31.610
Sometimes you just do it.
有时候你只能硬着头皮上。

147
00:06:31.990 --> 00:06:34.770
But I think everyone has some kind of a point.
但我觉得每个人都有点道理。

148
00:06:34.770 --> 00:06:38.070
You know, she has a point to feel embarrassed about that.
你知道的，她感到尴尬是有道理的。

149
00:06:38.310 --> 00:06:40.210
These people she doesn't know, knowing this intimate detail.
这些她并不认识的人，却知道了这么私密的细节。

150
00:06:40.430 --> 00:06:41.510
But Ted is right.
但泰德是对的。

151
00:06:41.670 --> 00:06:42.730
And you know Ted's right.
而且你知道泰德是对的。

152
00:06:42.930 --> 00:06:47.190
And I like Stella a lot for coming back after that fight and saying, you were right.
而且我很喜欢斯特拉在经历那场争吵后回来并说，你是对的。

153
00:06:47.390 --> 00:06:47.790
Yeah.
是的。

154
00:06:48.050 --> 00:06:53.190
And letting Ted in actually to a deeper level of intimacy than they were even talking about,
而且让泰德进入了比他们之前谈论的更深层次的亲密关系，

155
00:06:53.270 --> 00:06:55.110
