00:37:02.040 --> 00:37:04.620
Which is guys regret the girls they didn't sleep with.
那就是男生会后悔没有和那些女孩发生关系。

885
00:37:04.760 --> 00:37:06.560
Girls regret the guys they did sleep with.
而女孩会后悔和那些男生发生了关系。

886
00:37:06.580 --> 00:37:07.320
It's a killer line.
这台词太绝了。

887
00:37:07.660 --> 00:37:07.820
Yeah.
是啊。

888
00:37:08.000 --> 00:37:08.600
There's wisdom.
这里面有大智慧。

889
00:37:08.880 --> 00:37:10.240
That's a true line.
这话太对了。

890
00:37:10.640 --> 00:37:12.940
Everyone had a good point of view in this episode.
这一集里每个人的观点都很棒。

891
00:37:13.060 --> 00:37:15.560
That's why it was a juicy, except for like this little sweaty moment or two.
这就是为什么它很有看头，除了那一两个有点冒汗的小时刻。

892
00:37:15.900 --> 00:37:17.000
Everyone had a good argument.
每个人都有很好的论点。

893
00:37:17.200 --> 00:37:18.680
That's the most fun thing to write in the world.
这是世界上写起来最好玩的事情。

894
00:37:18.680 --> 00:37:22.060
Well, it's the kind of thing of the writer's thing, like everyone's right.
嗯，这就是那种编剧的秘诀，仿佛每个人都是对的。

895
00:37:22.540 --> 00:37:23.040
Everyone's right.
每个人都是对的。

896
00:37:23.440 --> 00:37:24.980
Eric Boghossian told me that years.
埃里克·博戈相多年前对我说过。

897
00:37:25.620 --> 00:37:28.580
My first job out of school was working on an Eric Boghossian play.
我毕业后的第一份工作就是在埃里克·博戈相的一部戏剧里工作。

898
00:37:28.720 --> 00:37:33.040
And he said my playwriting changed when I realized everyone had to be right all the time.
他说当他意识到每个人在任何时候都必须是正确的时，他的剧本创作就改变了。

899
00:37:33.200 --> 00:37:34.220
That's where the drama comes from.
戏剧冲突就是这么来的。

900
00:37:34.320 --> 00:37:39.060
As an actor, whatever your character you're playing, you find how they're right, right?
作为一名演员，无论你演的是什么角色，你都要找出他们合理的地方，对吧？

901
00:37:39.160 --> 00:37:42.560
Whether it's you, Josh Wagner doesn't have to agree with that character.
无论是不是你，乔什·瓦格纳不一定要认同那个角色。

902
00:37:42.560 --> 00:37:45.780
But you have to fight for your life in the midst of that.
但在那之中你必须为自己的生命而战。

903
00:37:45.940 --> 00:37:49.380
You have to give it your all and really be an advocate for their—
你必须全力以赴，真正成为他们——的拥护者

904
00:37:49.380 --> 00:37:50.340
It's almost like a lawyer.
这几乎就像个律师。

905
00:37:50.880 --> 00:37:52.280
Like, you get hired.
就像，你被雇用了。

906
00:37:52.600 --> 00:37:54.020
You're the lawyer for the character.
你是那个角色的律师。

907
00:37:54.240 --> 00:37:58.440
And you have to just—even if you don't agree with them, you've got to defend them with all your skill.
你必须——即使你不同意他们的观点，你也得用你全部的技巧去辩护。

908
00:37:58.680 --> 00:37:58.880
Right.
没错。

909
00:37:58.880 --> 00:38:02.480
They deserve a fair defense in court.
他们在法庭上应得一场公正的辩护。

910
00:38:02.480 --> 00:38:05.040
And in acting court, you give them that defense.
而在表演法庭上，你给了他们那样的辩护。

911
00:38:05.560 --> 00:38:06.900
And it's the same with writing.
写作也是一样。

912
00:38:07.400 --> 00:38:09.020
And, like, Stella has a point.
而且，就像，斯特拉说得有道理。

913
00:38:09.280 --> 00:38:12.340
She explains why she hasn't slept with him in five years, and it makes sense.
她解释了为什么她五年没和他睡过觉，这说得通。

914
00:38:12.560 --> 00:38:17.880
And she is mad at Ted in a way that I was team Ted, but I understood why she was mad at Ted.
而且她生泰ッド的气的方式——虽然我支持泰ッド，但我理解她为什么生泰ッド的气。

915
00:38:18.020 --> 00:38:18.900
And so it was interesting.
所以这很有趣。

916
00:38:19.180 --> 00:38:22.640
And if you were in her shoes, you'd be like, this is humiliating.
如果你处在她的立场，你会觉得，这太羞辱人了。

917
00:38:23.000 --> 00:38:25.020
I don't want people I don't know to know that, right?
我不想让不认识的人知道这些，对吧？

918
00:38:25.120 --> 00:38:26.060
I told you that.
我跟你说过这个。

919
00:38:26.440 --> 00:38:26.820
I know.
我知道。

920
00:38:26.940 --> 00:38:27.320
I know.
我知道。

921
00:38:27.320 --> 00:38:29.920
So she's right, but I also think Ted's right.
所以她是正确的，但我也觉得泰得是对的。

922
00:38:30.040 --> 00:38:32.240
I thought you were telling me that about you, Craig.
我还以为你是在跟我说你自己的事呢，克雷格。

923
00:38:33.060 --> 00:38:34.660
And I was like, I would never tell that on the air.
当时我想，我绝不会在节目里说这种事。

924
00:38:34.660 --> 00:38:35.680
Let's talk about this off mic.
我们关掉麦克风聊这个吧。

925
00:38:37.900 --> 00:38:39.220
Go do some personal stuff.
去聊点私事吧。

926
00:38:39.780 --> 00:38:47.880
One of Randy's favorite, one of my favorite Will Forte moments was, tonight is going to be legendary, wait for it, Gary.
兰迪最喜欢的、我最喜欢的威尔·福特的时刻之一就是，今晚注定会成为传奇，拭目以待吧，加里。

927
00:38:48.560 --> 00:38:49.460
Poor Randy.
可怜的兰迪。

928
00:38:49.760 --> 00:38:52.300
Poor Randy is having, he's just too excited.
可怜的兰迪，他实在是太激动了。

929
00:38:52.520 --> 00:38:53.960
He's just too lonely and excited.
他只是太孤独又太激动了。

930
00:38:54.220 --> 00:38:55.940
He wants to fit in so badly.
他太想融入大家了。

931
00:38:56.260 --> 00:38:56.600
Oh.
哦。

932
00:38:57.080 --> 00:38:57.560
Forte.
福特。

933
00:38:57.740 --> 00:39:00.100
No one could have done that better, that role, than Forte.
没有人能比福特把那个角色演得更好了。

934
00:39:00.100 --> 00:39:00.860
No, no, no, no.
不，不，不，不。

935
00:39:00.860 --> 00:39:01.320
It's perfect.
太完美了。

936
00:39:01.360 --> 00:39:02.300
Chiseled to perfection.
雕琢得近乎完美。

937
00:39:02.300 --> 00:39:10.680
And we knew we wanted Forte, and we waited for the perfect moment, and somehow it was in this nine-episode scramble of slapping this thing together that we're like, rebound, bro.
我们知道我们想要福特，我们等待着最佳时机，不知怎么的，就在我们仓促拼凑这九集节目的焦头烂额中，我们觉得，做接盘侠吧，兄弟。

938
00:39:11.000 --> 00:39:12.540
He will be Barney's rebound, bro.
他将成为巴尼的接盘侠，兄弟。

939
00:39:12.640 --> 00:39:15.560
And also, it's knowing that we are really good friends with Will.
而且，这也因为我们知道我们跟威尔是极好的朋友。

940
00:39:15.700 --> 00:39:17.000
Did you write it for Will?
你们是为威尔写的吗？

941
00:39:17.160 --> 00:39:19.620
Yeah, I think we very quickly had the idea of Will.
对，我想我们很快就有了找威尔的想法。

942
00:39:19.780 --> 00:39:23.340
And also, I mean, it helps to be able to like, we have to cast this in no time at all.
而且，我的意思是，这有好处，就像，我们必须在极短时间内完成选角。

943
00:39:23.600 --> 00:39:24.800
Let's call our friend Will.
我们给朋友威尔打个电话吧。

944
00:39:25.160 --> 00:39:25.560
Yeah, yeah, yeah.
对，对，对。

945
00:39:25.560 --> 00:39:26.580
And he's perfect for it.
而且他完美契合这个角色。

946
00:39:26.740 --> 00:39:31.640
So, there were a lot of stars aligned in the making of these nine episodes,
所以，制作这九集节目时可以说是天时地利人和，

947
00:39:31.860 --> 00:39:42.400
including from Britney Spears to Sarah Chalk somehow being able to do this in her five free minutes a day from Scrubs to Will Forte just being a great friend and the perfect person for this part.
从布兰妮·斯皮尔斯到莎拉·乔克居然能从《实习医生风云》每天仅有的五分钟空闲里抽出时间来演，再到威尔·福特既是个好朋友又是这个角色的完美人选。

948
00:39:43.060 --> 00:39:46.660
Goddamn, a lot of things had to work for these nine episodes to exiSt.
天呐，这九集节目要想存在，必须得有好多事情同时顺利运转才行。

949
00:39:47.280 --> 00:39:51.620
Where did you, who came up with, he gets a nosebleed when he has an erection?
你们是在哪——是谁想出来的，他勃起时会流鼻血这个设定？

950
00:39:52.100 --> 00:39:54.480
I feel that might have been a Jamie Ronheimer pitch.
我感觉这可能是杰米·罗恩海默的点子。

951
00:39:54.480 --> 00:40:00.440
I just, he might have, I, I, I can't remember if it was in his draft or he pitched it in the room, but I think, I think that might have, I remember,
我只是，他可能，我，我，我不记得这是在他的初稿里还是他在房间里提出来的，但我觉得，我觉得那可能，我记得，

952
00:40:00.540 --> 00:40:05.800
I feel like I remember Jamie saying, I'm sorry, I get a nosebleed, this happens every time I get an erection.
我觉得我记得杰米说过，对不起，我流鼻血了，我每次勃起都会这样。

953
00:40:06.040 --> 00:40:10.600
And like, just it being the weirdest, because you're, part of what's funny about the joke is like,
而且就像，这简直是最诡异的，因为你，这个笑话好笑的一部分就在于，

954
00:40:10.780 --> 00:40:15.420
your brain immediately scrambles to figure out the physiological underpinnings of that.
你的大脑会立刻开始拼命去理清其中的生理基础。

955
00:40:16.020 --> 00:40:22.600
Well, it's also like, getting a nosebleed when you're trying to talk to a woman is already like, unnerving.
对，而且就像，当你试图跟一个女人说话时流鼻血，本来就已经让人，心里发毛了。

956
00:40:22.920 --> 00:40:23.760
It's so unnerving.
太让人心里发毛了。

957
00:40:23.760 --> 00:40:24.700
It's so unnerving.
太让人心里发毛了。

958
00:40:25.060 --> 00:40:31.280
And then the revelation that physiologically, this is what happens when I get into, it's like, oh my God, this poor guy.
然后发现从生理上讲，当我进入状态时就会这样，就好像，天哪，这个可怜的家伙。

959
00:40:31.480 --> 00:40:33.020
He needs to go to a hospital right now.
他现在得去医院。

960
00:40:35.560 --> 00:40:37.100
I'm very worried about Randy.
我很为兰迪担心。

961
00:40:38.220 --> 00:40:39.720
But no one's funnier.
但没有人比他更好笑了。

962
00:40:39.840 --> 00:40:47.060
I think also it was partially just the joy of like, Will Forte having a nosebleed is going to be funny, because he's going to be so committed and undeterred.
我觉得还有一部分纯粹是因为那种快乐，威尔·福特流鼻血肯定会很好笑，因为他会表现得那么投入、那么坚决。

963
00:40:47.640 --> 00:40:49.800
He's so not going to care about looking insane.
他绝对不会在乎自己看起来有多疯狂。

964
00:40:50.040 --> 00:40:54.180
When he has that second nosebleed and kind of has smeared it all over his face.
当他流第二次鼻血的时候，把血抹了满脸都是。

965
00:40:54.360 --> 00:40:55.320
And turns around to smile.
然后转过身来笑。

966
00:40:55.560 --> 00:40:57.200
And takes the nap down to say, thank to Mal, thank you to Barney.
把纸巾拿下来，对马尔说，谢谢巴尼，谢谢你。

967
00:40:57.340 --> 00:41:00.600
And he's just covered in blood like it's a fucking Scorsese film.
而他满脸是血，就像在拍他妈的斯科塞斯电影一样。

968
00:41:00.700 --> 00:41:01.480
But what does Barney say?
但巴尼说什么来着？

969
00:41:01.540 --> 00:41:03.200
It's like an old bullet wound or something?
就好像是个旧子弹伤什么的？

970
00:41:03.500 --> 00:41:03.920
Yeah, whatever.
对，随便啦。

971
00:41:04.060 --> 00:41:06.160
Barney's given a good backstory of what that is.
巴尼为那是什么编了一个很好的背景故事。

972
00:41:06.740 --> 00:41:10.560
And yeah, a bullet is lodged in his sinuses, I think is what Barney said.
对啊，一颗子弹卡在他的鼻窦里了，巴尼好像是这么说的。

973
00:41:11.160 --> 00:41:15.460
But Will's sweet little thank you while he's covered in blood.
但威尔满脸是血时那种甜甜的感谢。

974
00:41:15.660 --> 00:41:19.680
That image, I think we just knew Forte, that image of Forte was going to be funny.
那个画面，我想我们当时就知道福特，福特那个画面肯定会很好笑。

975
00:41:19.840 --> 00:41:20.460
And it's juSt...
而且简直……

976
00:41:20.460 --> 00:41:22.420
And then you think about Monday at the office.
然后你就会想到周一在办公室的情景。

977
00:41:22.740 --> 00:41:33.240
If Barney wasn't already, like, iconically, the man to Randy is going to forever be enshrined as like the greatest person.
如果巴尼本身还不是的话，在兰迪心目中，这个男人将永远被奉为最伟大的人。

978
00:41:33.280 --> 00:41:34.020
It's a success story.
这是一个成功的故事。

979
00:41:34.020 --> 00:41:37.000
This is an underdog story, and it happens.
这是一个逆袭的故事，而且它发生了。

980
00:41:37.260 --> 00:41:38.740
And Barney's really proud of him.
巴尼为他感到非常骄傲。

981
00:41:38.960 --> 00:41:40.700
And then Robin says, Ted doesn't know.
然后罗宾说，泰德还不知道。

982
00:41:40.800 --> 00:41:41.840
So you are a great wingman.
所以你是个出色的僚机。

983
00:41:42.020 --> 00:41:43.100
Ted doesn't know what he's missing out on.
泰德根本不知道自己错过了什么。

984
00:41:43.160 --> 00:41:44.520
You had to mention Ted.
你非得提泰德。

985
00:41:44.680 --> 00:41:45.540
And Barney's back in tears.
然后巴尼又开始哭了。

986
00:41:45.700 --> 00:41:46.340
Which I love.
这我太喜欢了。

987
00:41:46.420 --> 00:41:51.500
It was funny, but also reminded you of what the stakes of this whole arc are.
这很有趣，但也让你想起了这整条故事线所面临的利害关系。

988
00:41:52.180 --> 00:41:54.020
And nothing has been solved.
而且什么问题都还没解决。

989
00:41:54.260 --> 00:41:57.600
We still have this ongoing condition of this big problem for the group.
我们依然要面对这个团队一直存在的大问题。

990
00:41:57.700 --> 00:41:58.460
I like that.
我挺喜欢那段的。

991
00:41:58.660 --> 00:42:02.080
It almost feels like Barney is like Mickey from Rocky.
感觉巴尼就像《洛奇》里的米奇。

992
00:42:02.080 --> 00:42:04.620
Rocky, and he, like, loses his prize fighter.
洛奇，然后他，就像是失去了他的拳王。

993
00:42:04.740 --> 00:42:09.360
And he has to find another guy at the gym to train because he doesn't know who he is unless he's training a fighter.
他不得不去健身房找另一个人来训练，因为如果他不训练一个拳手，他都不知道自己是谁了。

994
00:42:09.360 --> 00:42:14.800
I just rewatched Rocky because we were going to go visit Philadelphia for the first time.
我刚重温了《洛奇》，因为我们打算第一次去费城参观。

995
00:42:15.220 --> 00:42:17.420
And Rebecca, my wife, had never seen Rocky.
而我的妻子丽贝卡以前从没看过《洛奇》。

996
00:42:17.680 --> 00:42:19.380
And we watched Rocky.
我们看了《洛奇》。

997
00:42:19.700 --> 00:42:23.240
First of all, she was, like, an hour and ten minutes into the movie.
首先，她看了电影一个多小时以后，

998
00:42:23.300 --> 00:42:26.240
She's like, when's there going to be some goddamn boxing in this movie?
她就说，这电影到底什么时候才能有该死的拳击场面啊？

999
00:42:26.340 --> 00:42:28.580
Because it's, like, really this little character piece.
因为这其实是一部非常细腻的人物刻画片。

1000
00:42:28.740 --> 00:42:30.360
But kind of in a great way, though.
不过话说回来，这也挺棒的。

1001
00:42:30.420 --> 00:42:32.160
She didn't even mean it as a diss, really.
她其实甚至都不是故意贬低。

1002
00:42:32.260 --> 00:42:35.020
It's, like, it is an interesting character portrait, that movie.
而且怎么说呢，那部电影确实是个很有趣的人物画像。

1003
00:42:35.100 --> 00:42:36.020
It's really a good movie.
真的是部好电影。

1004
00:42:37.200 --> 00:42:38.180
But what's so interesting.
但最有趣的地方在于。

1005
00:42:38.240 --> 00:42:43.180
The electric boogaloos of that series really changed what the original was.
那个系列的《霹雳舞续集》真的改变了原作的内核。

1006
00:42:43.180 --> 00:42:47.120
Like, the first one is, like, the first one won the Academy Award.
比如，第一部，第一部可是赢得过奥斯卡奖的。

1007
00:42:47.640 --> 00:42:49.220
I think it beat Taxi Driver.
我觉得它打败了《出租车司机》。

1008
00:42:49.660 --> 00:42:50.560
It beat something big.
它打败了一部大片。

1009
00:42:50.680 --> 00:42:51.480
Oh, you're right about that.
哦，你这话没错。

1010
00:42:51.640 --> 00:42:56.200
The one that sticks in my head is the fact that Sylvester Stallone won the Oscar for Best Screenplay.
最让我印象深刻的是，西尔维斯特·史泰龙居然凭《洛奇》赢得了最佳编剧奖。

1011
00:42:56.240 --> 00:42:56.460
Best Screenplay.
最佳编剧奖。

1012
00:42:56.720 --> 00:42:58.440
Which people forget, and it's kind of amazing.
很多人都忘了这一点，而且这简直太神奇了。

1013
00:42:58.920 --> 00:42:59.780
Well, he wrote his ticket.
嗯，他靠这个一举成名了。

1014
00:43:00.120 --> 00:43:05.560
Okay, it beat all the President's Men, Network, and Taxi Driver.
好吧，它击败了《总统班底》、《电视台风云》和《出租车司机》。

1015
00:43:05.560 --> 00:43:14.420
I mean, that thing was, one of my favorite things about re-watching Rocky was Mickey, Burgess Meredith, the trainer.
我的意思是，重看《洛奇》时我最喜欢的事情之一就是米奇，也就是伯吉斯·梅雷迪思饰演的那个教练。

1016
00:43:15.300 --> 00:43:17.280
He, again, everyone has a thing.
他呢，还是那句话，每个人都有自己的小心思。

1017
00:43:17.480 --> 00:43:19.240
And this is why it was good writing and good acting.
这就是为什么这剧本好、演技也好。

1018
00:43:19.620 --> 00:43:27.600
Burgess Meredith really has denied Rocky the whole movie and shunned him and not taken him under his wing.
伯吉斯·梅雷迪思在整部电影里一直对洛奇爱答不理，甚至排斥他，也从没把收他为徒。

1019
00:43:27.760 --> 00:43:33.020
The second Rocky is now the new hot thing, now Burgess Meredith kind of comes knocking on Rocky's door.
而当《洛奇2》里洛奇成了新晋红人时，伯吉斯·梅雷迪思却主动敲响了洛奇的门。

1020
00:43:33.020 --> 00:43:37.800
And Rocky tears him a new one and says, you were not there for me for all of these years.
结果洛奇把他骂得狗血淋头，说你这些年根本不管我死活。

1021
00:43:37.860 --> 00:43:40.920
And you're just trying to get something out of me because you're washed up.
你现在来找我只是想从我这儿捞点好处，因为你已经过气了。

1022
00:43:41.060 --> 00:43:43.880
And it's, like, so great because you realize Rocky's right.
这情节太棒了，因为你意识到洛奇说得完全对。

1023
00:43:44.300 --> 00:43:46.620
Burgess Meredith is, like, this is my last chance.
伯吉斯·梅雷迪思则一副这是我最后机会的样子。

1024
00:43:46.620 --> 00:43:48.560
I'm this hunched-over old man.
我只是个驼着背的老头子。

1025
00:43:48.720 --> 00:43:49.360
This is it.
就是这样了。

1026
00:43:49.680 --> 00:43:51.440
I need this last little thing.
我太需要这最后的机会了。

1027
00:43:51.600 --> 00:43:52.900
And it's always great.
这种桥段总是百看不厌。

1028
00:43:53.460 --> 00:43:55.380
I don't know, Barney had that energy.
我不知道，巴尼当时就是那种状态。

1029
00:43:55.500 --> 00:44:01.200
So, in this metaphor, Barney is Burgess Meredith and Randy Warmpiss is Rocky Balboa.
所以在这个比喻里，巴尼就是伯吉斯·梅雷迪思，而兰迪·沃姆皮斯就是洛奇·巴尔博亚。

1030
00:44:01.200 --> 00:44:03.500
Absolutely, absolutely, absolutely.
完全赞同，完全赞同，完全赞同。

1031
00:44:03.960 --> 00:44:12.860
And Barney is trying to redeem himself in the way that Burgess Meredith is trying to find redemption through Rocky, having not earned that with Rocky at all.
巴尼试图救赎自己，就像伯吉斯·梅雷迪思试图通过洛奇来获得救赎一样，尽管他之前根本没为洛奇付出过什么。

1032
00:44:12.920 --> 00:44:17.520
Because he only gets with Rocky when Rocky has this insane chance.
因为他只有在洛奇拥有疯狂机遇的时候才会贴上来。

1033
00:44:17.840 --> 00:44:18.480
I just love it.
我太爱这个设定了。

1034
00:44:18.540 --> 00:44:22.560
I think good writing is always when it's, like, everyone has a thing, everyone has an angle.
我觉得优秀的剧本总是这样，每个人都有自己的小九九，每个人都有自己的盘算。

1035
00:44:22.860 --> 00:44:25.040
Burgess Meredith is not the wise old trainer.
伯吉斯·梅雷迪思才不是什么慈祥的智者老教练。

1036
00:44:25.180 --> 00:44:28.180
He's sort of a washed-up guy who goes, this is my last chance at a win.
他其实是个过气的家伙，心里想的是这是我咸鱼翻身的最后机会。

1037
00:44:28.180 --> 00:44:29.260
And it's great.
这设定太棒了。

1038
00:44:29.880 --> 00:44:39.540
And I like that Barney is just, like, really trying to get redemption out of—he's trying to make amends to the universe by getting this sad sack guy laid.
我喜欢巴尼那种死皮赖脸寻求救赎的感觉——他试图通过帮这个悲催的家伙破处来向宇宙弥补过失。

1039
00:44:39.680 --> 00:44:45.920
And he does it, but it doesn't fill the hole in his life, the Left by Ted, which is great.
他确实做到了，但这并没有填补他心中由特德离去留下的空洞，这设定真的很绝。

1040
00:44:46.540 --> 00:44:48.380
And that's the condition we're going to come back to.
这就是我们接下来要回归的状态。

1041
00:44:57.880 --> 00:45:03.560
